    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, that's better, the empathy is definitely there. \n\nbut the sentiment engine is still flagging it as quite low (it's sitting at like 0.3). for this specific campaign, our stakeholders are really pushing for a more \"uplifting\" feel to drive customer loyalty. they want to see that score get into the 0.6-0.7 range.\n\ni'm still really worried about it sounding fake or sarcastic—like \"yay, you're broke!\"—so please, keep it grounded. but can you look for ways to use more positive/supportive language so we can bump that score up? maybe focus more on the \"solutions\" and \"support\" side of things to get that metric higher.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
